Copyright 2026 Andreas Kruse (Sprinterli)

This product includes the betterleaks ruleset (maisecrets/rules/betterleaks.toml),
Copyright (c) 2026 Zachary Rice, MIT License (see maisecrets/rules/LICENSE-betterleaks),
consumed as data. The vendored version is recorded in maisecrets/rules/BETTERLEAKS_VERSION.
Its filter expressions are read by maisecrets/rule_filter.py.

maisecrets' own secret rules (maisecrets/rules/own_secret_rules.json) are derived from patterns
of the gitleaks ruleset v8.30.1, Copyright (c) 2019 Zachary Rice, MIT License (see
maisecrets/rules/LICENSE-gitleaks). gitleaks itself is no longer vendored.

This product includes PII detection patterns derived from Microsoft Presidio
(maisecrets/rules/presidio.json: regexes, scores and context words of its
pattern recognizers), Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation, MIT License (see
maisecrets/rules/LICENSE-presidio). The checksum validators for the generic
and German entities in maisecrets/detect.py are ports of Presidio's, verified
by scripts/check_validators_against_presidio.py.

This product includes regular expressions derived from Yelp detect-secrets
(maisecrets/rules/detect_secrets.json: the KeywordDetector and
BasicAuthDetector patterns), Copyright Yelp, Inc., Apache License 2.0 (see
maisecrets/rules/LICENSE-detect-secrets). Its heuristic filters for keyword
hits are ported in maisecrets/detect.py.

This product includes a word list created from SCOWL (maisecrets/rules/words_en.txt: the base
words of 4 to 8 letters of the en_US Hunspell dictionary, SCOWL size 60, release rel-2026.02.25,
https://github.com/en-wl/wordlist/releases/tag/rel-2026.02.25), Copyright 2000-2026 by Kevin
Atkinson, under the SCOWL license (a permissive license; see maisecrets/rules/LICENSE-scowl).
scripts/sync_words.py rebuilds it from the pinned release asset and records the version in
maisecrets/rules/SCOWL_VERSION. The password rule uses it to tell a word from a password.

The remaining rules in maisecrets/detect.py (OWN_RULES, REGIONAL_RULES), maisecrets/checksums.py
and the display rules in maisecrets/pii_display.py are written for this project.

Parts of the detection are adapted from a public fork of maisecrets on GitHub (Apache License
2.0; the commits that took them name it): the card words of other
languages, the IBAN forms with hyphens and in lower case, the context rule for a bare German VAT ID,
the normaliser of maisecrets/normalise.py (changed: five of its stages, one module, scanned
only around the changed lines and in the tool channel only), the design of the country rules
(REGIONAL_RULES in maisecrets/detect.py) and the checksums of the AHV number, the Swiss UID and the
codice fiscale in maisecrets/checksums.py.
